-- The Eliot test framework as a package.
--
-- **The root package is the framework and nothing else**: `src/` at `.`, the assertions, the mocks and
-- the runner's module, with no platform and no `compiler` line. Both absences are load-bearing. A
-- framework is as platform-independent as what it tests, and a consumer inheriting `//jvm` from here
-- could never build for anything else; and a line on `root` would run in every closure holding the
-- framework, `runner` among them.
--
-- **`suite` is what a consumer's test package deps.** It is `root` plus the one line that runs a suite:
-- `compiler run -m eliot.test.Runner` compiles the closure with the runner as its entry point and then
-- runs it, exiting with its code. It names no backend — the one backend in the consumer's closure that
-- accepts `run` gets it — so the line stays as platform-independent as the framework. A consumer writes
-- `dep github.com/eliotlang/eliot-test//suite v0.2` beside its platform and `eliot build test` runs its
-- cases. `suite` has no sources of its own; its directory does not exist and mounts nothing.
--
-- Both layers of the base are named in `root`, because `src` resolves against what it declares and
-- nothing else: the assertions and the mocks are written over `eliot.collection.List`, `eliot.file` and
-- `eliot.system`, and the runner reaches every suite in a program through `eliot.compiler.Reflect`,
-- which the `lang` layer declares rather than `stdlib`.
--
-- `runner` is the executable this repository ships: the same entry point, built rather than run. `test`
-- is this repository's own suite, at `test/src`, and it runs the way every consumer's does — through
-- `//suite`.
--
-- `v0.4` is the floor because it is the first eliot tag whose compiler has the `run` mode and picks a
-- backend by it, and whose descriptor names its assets the way a launcher reads today.

-- The launcher `./eliotw` runs, and the one line of this file the wrapper reads: it greps for the first
-- line starting `launcher `. The launcher itself accepts the line and ignores it.
launcher v0.3

package root {
  at .
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//lang v0.4
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//stdlib v0.4
}

package suite {
  dep //root
  compiler run -m eliot.test.Runner
}

package runner {
  dep //root
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//jvm v0.4
  compiler exe-jar -m eliot.test.Runner
}

package test {
  dep //suite
  dep github.com/robertbraeutigam/eliot//jvm v0.4
}
